<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK ELECTRICAL UTILITY SE H1 PROFIT DIPS.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK ELECTRICAL UTILITY SE H1 PROFIT DIPS.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six-month period</p>
<p>ending June 30, 1997: (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit			2.814     vs     3.087</p>
<p> Operating revenues		 15.339     vs    14.862</p>
<p> Operating costs		    12.213     vs    11.512</p>
<p> Operating profit		    3.125     vs     3.350</p>
<p>Revenues from financial</p>
<p>  operations			   0.280     vs     0.190</p>
<p> Financial costs		     0.648     vs     0.468</p>
<p>Results from financial</p>
<p>  operations			  -0.368     vs    -0.277</p>
<p> Total loans			  28.716     vs    21.277</p>
<p>  Long-term loans		   28.329     vs    16.796</p>
<p>  Short-term loans		   0.387     vs     4.480</p>
<p> Reserves				0.806     vs     0.307</p>
<p> Basic capital			41.804     vs    40.289</p>
<p> Total assets			101.869     vs    82.072</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Slovenske Elektrarne a.s. (SE).</p>
<p>SE is a wholly state-owned energy monopoly. It is included on</p>
<p>the government's list of strategic companies excluded from</p>
<p>privatisation.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 421-7-521-8402</p>
</text>
